sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py; output: docs/media/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587; artifact_sha256: 68bcaffb42002b53f8666b482f0c8eb740fd840065dd289e2b5fd57b6ee1fefd; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Brodland (2002) J. Biomech. Eng. Eqs. 1-4: Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) decomposing cell-cell interfacial tension into actomyosin cortical tension minus cadherin adhesion (gamma_{alpha,beta} = beta_alpha + beta_beta - omega_{alpha,beta}). | Krieg et al. (2008) Nature Cell Biology Figs. 1-4: AFM cortical tension hierarchy across zebrafish shield-stage germ-layer progenitors (beta_ectoderm ~ 50 < beta_mesoderm ~ 95 < beta_endoderm ~ 130 pN/um), concentric 3-germ-layer sorting, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition arrest, and caMLCK ectodermal cortical stiffening sorting reversal. | Maître et al. (2012) Science Eq. 1: Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle cos(theta) = 1 - gamma_cc/(2*gamma_cm) and normalized contact radius r_c/R = sin(theta).; reconstructed_in_script: 2D deformable DITH cell sorting across all 4 perturbation regimes (wild-type engulfment, caMLCK cortex reversal, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition, and high-HIT mushroom doublet) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446), a 7-point continuous beta_E sweep across the sorting inversion threshold beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um, and the Young-Dupré doublet contact curve. | Computer-vision segmentation of zebrafish blastoderm cross-transplantation GFP/RFP micrographs (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`) across both layered engulfment (Row B, radial profile r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844) and the protruding mushroom doublet (Row C, empirical r_c/R = 0.9717).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice DITH representation of 3D zebrafish germ-layer progenitor reaggregates and blastoderm cross-transplants.; does_not_claim: Does not model sub-second single-molecule E-cadherin bond rupture kinetics or whole-embryo epiboly yolk-syncytial-layer microtubule pulling.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1705>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00146-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704252104>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.1449491>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1225399> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.913"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "b9976f8" .
}

